From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:55:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] H21: keep the reference words while a refinement's
 reference column is negative

With a positive GRREFERENCEDX the reference column under the first pixels
of a row (x - dx) is left of the reference. maybe_reload_buffers then
zeroed the three reference words that start_row had loaded at column 0 and
left their start at 0, and its reload test (ref_x + 1 >= start + 32, or
ref_x < start) stayed false until ref_x reached 31. Reference columns 0-30,
and the template's right-hand pixel at ref_x = -1, therefore read as white,
so every refinement placed right of its reference (text-region and
symbol-dictionary refinements included) decoded to other pixels, with or
without typical prediction, which reads the same words. Negative offsets,
either vertical offset and the right edge were unaffected.

Leave the column-0 words in place while the column is negative: pixels left
of the reference already read as 0 through the wrapped offset, column 0 is
where the right-hand pixel lands at ref_x = -1, and the words serve until
the existing test reloads them at ref_x = 31.

New round-trip tests code noisy targets against noisy references with the
test kit's MQ encoder at (1, 0), (1, 1) and (1, -1), at a size that crosses
two word boundaries as well, with the offsets that already decoded as a
control.

Fixes internal #115
---
 hayro-jbig2/src/decode/generic_refinement.rs | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hayro-jbig2/src/decode/generic_refinement.rs b/hayro-jbig2/src/decode/generic_refinement.rs
index cfc4b18..d6d513f 100644
--- a/hayro-jbig2/src/decode/generic_refinement.rs
+++ b/hayro-jbig2/src/decode/generic_refinement.rs
@@ -260,13 +260,15 @@ impl<'a> RefinementContextGatherer<'a> {
             self.reg_cur = ContextGatherer::load_word(region, self.reg_y, new_start);
         }
 
+        // While the reference column is left of the reference (a positive
+        // GRREFERENCEDX), keep the words `start_row` loaded at column 0: the
+        // template's right-hand pixel reaches column 0 at ref_x = -1, columns
+        // further left read as 0 through the wrapped offset, and the words
+        // stay valid until ref_x reaches 31. Zeroing them here, as before,
+        // read reference columns 0-30 as white, because the test below does
+        // not reload until then.
         let ref_x_signed = x as i32 - self.reference_dx;
-        if ref_x_signed < 0 {
-            self.ref_cur_x = 0;
-            self.ref_m1 = 0;
-            self.ref_cur = 0;
-            self.ref_p1 = 0;
-        } else {
+        if ref_x_signed >= 0 {
             let ref_x = ref_x_signed as u32;
 
             if ref_x + 1 >= self.ref_cur_x + WORD_BITS || ref_x < self.ref_cur_x {
